@page "/privacy"

@* Public privacy policy (Spec A-15, issue #680). A legal document: wording changes need the
   owner's sign-off, and SiteIdentity.PoliciesLastUpdated must move with them. Keep the texting
   paragraph consistent with /sms-terms, and the retention paragraph with RVS_Spec.md A-15. *@

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy</PageTitle>

<MudStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Class="mt-8">
    <MudPaper Elevation="2" Class="pa-6 rounded-lg" Style="width: 100%; max-width: 640px;">
        <MudStack Spacing="3">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">RV Intake privacy policy</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Style="color: var(--mud-palette-text-secondary);">
                Last updated @SiteIdentity.PoliciesLastUpdated
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Who we are</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                RV Intake is a product of @SiteIdentity.LegalEntityName ("we", "us"). RV dealerships and
                RV service businesses use it to collect service requests from their customers. When you fill
                in the intake form, you are sending a request to the dealership named on the form, and we
                handle your information on that dealership's behalf.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">What we collect</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">When you submit a service request, we collect:</MudText>
            <ul>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Your contact details: name, email address, mobile number, how you prefer to be contacted, and whether you have opted out of texts or email.</MudText></li>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Details of your RV: VIN, make, model, year, warranty and approximate purchase date.</MudText></li>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Your description of the problem and your answers to the follow-up questions.</MudText></li>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Any photos, videos or audio files you attach.</MudText></li>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Voice input, if you use the microphone. The recording is converted to text for the form and is not kept.</MudText></li>
                <li><MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Technical information: your IP address, used to limit abuse, and which link you used to reach the form.</MudText></li>
            </ul>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">How we use it</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                We use your information to deliver your service request to the dealership, to send you a
                confirmation and status updates by text or email, and to run the status page linked from
                your confirmation. We use automated tools, including AI, to read your VIN from a photo,
                convert speech to text, suggest a problem category and follow-up questions, and prepare a
                preliminary assessment for the dealership. These suggestions are advisory. The dealership
                decides what work is done.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Who receives it</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                <b>The dealership</b> you are requesting service from receives your request and everything
                you submit with it. We also rely on service providers that process data for us only to run
                RV Intake: Microsoft Azure (hosting, storage, AI processing, and text and email delivery).
                Your VIN is sent to the U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration's public VIN
                decoder to look up your RV's details.
            </MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                We do not sell your personal information. We do not share it with third parties for their
                marketing. We disclose it otherwise only where the law requires us to.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Text messages</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                Your mobile number is used only to send the messages described in our
                <MudLink Href="/sms-terms" Typo="Typo.body1">texting terms</MudLink>. It is not sold or shared
                with third parties for marketing. Reply <b>STOP</b> to any message to stop receiving texts.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">How long we keep it</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                Your contact details and service requests are kept for as long as the dealership uses
                RV Intake, or until you ask us to delete them. We keep a service history for each RV,
                identified by its VIN, indefinitely: the vehicle's details, the problem category and
                description, and the date. We may use that history, with anything that identifies you,
                the dealership or any other person removed, to produce aggregated statistics.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Your choices</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                You can opt out of texts at any time by replying <b>STOP</b>, or opt out of texts or email
                when you fill in the form. To see, correct or delete the information we hold about you,
                email us at the address below or contact the dealership handling your request.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Security</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                Information is encrypted in transit and at rest. Each dealership can see only its own
                customers' requests.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Children</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                RV Intake is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their
                information.
            </MudText>

            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Changes and contact</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                If we change this policy, we will post the new version here with a new date. Questions or
                requests: <MudLink Href="@SiteIdentity.ContactMailto" Typo="Typo.body1">@SiteIdentity.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
            </MudText>
        </MudStack>
    </MudPaper>
</MudStack>
